 we get really  hyped up for going north of the wall but  in reality most of the scenes aren't  that fun or entertaining and generally  feature characters brooding around  forced labor at crasters and lots of  walking and digging but the whole  setting is very immersive and offers up  some breathtaking set pieces so at least  the visuals are wonderful things do get  really good when eager shows up and that  doesn't happen until the last half of  the season i do adore how she perfectly  challenges jon snow's ideals and their  debates about what makes someone free  like how jon snow swore an oath and now  he can never make love again the subplot  does end with a great climax of corn  half and sacrificing himself so jon can  win the trust of the free folk it's just  a shame that the first half of the  season jon doesn't have much to do  lastly we have daenerys and as i said  before her subplot this season is a bit  lackluster similar to jon's subplot the  first four episodes are mostly her  bumbling around in the desert until she  finds carth so naturally this in  comparison to something like season 3  where she's getting the unsullied will  be objectively worse even in qarth the  main conflict dany encounters isn't  amazing because a solution to her  problem is very convenient since sir joy  finds an all-knowing lady who never  comes back into the story and her powers  are never explained so as it stands it  feels like david and dan use quothi as a  cheap mcguffin plot device to move the  story forward besides those flaws  daenerys story still ends with a banger  by seeing visions and being revisited by  a fake khal drogo the sacrifice she  makes to leave him in her ultimate  paradise is heartbreaking and acts as a  great metaphor of leaving the past  behind to become the mother of dragons  so despite john and daenerys having some  flawed aspects in their stories they  still have some good qualities that  don't make their season 2 plot lines bad  by any means  so all together from the excellent  dialogue scenes are drenched in intrigue  dialogue that has also submerged in  tension the outstanding blackwater and  king's landing plotline the  interconnected and epic sense of the  battle of the five kings and some superb  plotlines makes season 2 great thank you  for watching and i'll try not to take  another big break for making the season  3 analysis
 

